From: OCCTSwift ecosystem <noreply@secondmouse.au>
Subject: [PATCH] Modeling Data - The shape readers refuse a count the stream cannot supply, and a
 reference outside its table

The text and binary shape readers (BRepTools_ShapeSet, TopTools_LocationSet, GeomTools_CurveSet,
Curve2dSet and SurfaceSet, Poly, BinTools_ShapeSet, CurveSet, Curve2dSet, SurfaceSet, LocationSet
and ShapeReader) size an array from a count the file declares, before the first element has been
read, and trust the count. The library is built with No_Exception, so the range checks of
NCollection_Array1, NCollection_Array2 and NCollection_IndexedMap are gone, and a damaged count
is not refused anywhere:
 - a negative count sizes an array backwards: a pole, knot or node count of a B-spline curve or
   surface, a triangulation or a polygon read as a negative number faulted in the constructor of
   the array or of the object built from it (Geom_BSplineCurve, Geom_BSplineSurface,
   Poly_Triangulation). In 76,479 single byte replacements of the text corpus, 22 did this, each a
   '-' where a digit was (12 in a curve record, 8 in a surface record, 2 in a triangulation).
 - a count past the end of the stream sizes an array of that many elements (2^31 - 1 poles is a
   50 GB array) and then runs its loop to the end, though the stream failed at the first element.
 - the two counts of a pole grid are each fine and their product overflows an int: a Bezier or
   B-spline surface of 65536 by 65536 poles.
 - a triangle names the nodes of its triangulation by index, and none is checked against the
   triangulation, nor is a polygon on a triangulation against the nodes that triangulation has.
 - a location entry names another and a power to raise it to. TopLoc_Location::Powered raises a
   composed location one multiplication at a time, recursively, so a power of 10^8 ends at the end
   of the stack (TopTools_LocationSet::Read, BinTools_LocationSet::Read and
   BinTools_ShapeReader::ReadLocation). A power beyond 4096 of a composed location is refused; a
   written file raises single locations only, which Powered takes in one step.

A reference from an edge or a face to a table is not checked in the places that name a polygon
or a triangulation: BRepTools_ShapeSet for a face that holds only a triangulation
(myTriangulations.FindKey(s)), BinTools_ShapeSet for the Polygon3D, PolygonOnTriangulation and
Triangulation of an edge and a face (myPolygons3D(c), myNodes(pt), myTriangulations.FindKey(t)),
BinTools_CurveSet, Curve2dSet and SurfaceSet for a curve and a surface, BinTools_LocationSet for
a location and BinTools_ShapeSet::ReadSubs for a sub-shape, none of which carry the range check
GeomTools_*Set and TopTools_LocationSet already have.

One rule: a count is refused when it is negative, or when the characters or bytes the stream
still holds cannot hold it, before any array is sized from it. Standard_IStreamHasItems(stream,
count, minimum size of an item) in Standard_IStream.hxx answers it. It refuses a negative count
and a failed stream; allows a count of 4096 or less without a look, since the reader stops at the
first element that is missing; measures a larger one against the rest of the stream (tellg and
seekg, restored); and, for a stream that cannot be measured, allows up to 2^24. A well-formed
file is read as before: the minimum is a lower bound (one character and a separator for a text
number, the size of the type for a binary one).

Failure is reported the way each reader already reports it: a failed stream and a null result
from the text readers (the table is left as it was, which the next table then finds failed),
Standard_Failure from the binary ones. A reference outside its table is skipped, as the text
readers already skip a Polygon3D and a PolygonOnTriangulation that the table does not hold; a
sub-shape or a location outside the binary table is refused, as TopTools_ShapeSet::Read already
refuses it. A triangle with a node the triangulation does not have, and a polygon with a node the
triangulation it is attached to does not have, are refused.

Tracked as SecondMouseAU/OCCTSwift#3490, follow-up to #3487, #3489 and the patch that stops the
text readers at a failed stream.

